course: dictionary
lesson: 7848
title: Radical: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word first. «The council plans a radical change to the park» is about a huge change, so radical means very big and basic. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Maths and science use the same word in their own ways. In maths, the radical sign √ shows a square root, so √16 = 4. In science, a free radical is an atom or group of atoms that reacts easily. Only the sentence can tell you which meaning you need.
explain: Slang can shorten a word. «"Rad", short for radical, was 1970s and 1980s American surfer and skater slang for excellent.» The full word radical still means a very big or extreme change, so do not mix up the short slang word with the full one.
fact: Radical has several meanings, so check the context before you choose one.
fact: A radical change is a very big change that alters the most important parts of something.
fact: Radical can also describe someone with very strong, extreme ideas about how society or politics should change.
fact: In maths, the radical sign √ shows a square root: √16 = 4.
fact: «Rad» is American slang for excellent, short for radical, used in the 1970s and 1980s.
exercise: «The new school rules made a radical change to how we learn.» What does radical mean here? | A small tidy-up of the classroom | Something that happens only once, very quickly | *Very big and basic, changing the most important parts | A square root sign
exercise: In maths, the sign √ is called the ___ sign. | *radical | percent | decimal | fraction
exercise: «"Rad", short for radical, was 1970s slang for excellent.» What does rad mean? | A square root | A very big change | A person with extreme political ideas | *Excellent
test: In «The radicals wanted fast change», what are the radicals? | A kind of tree | *People with very strong, extreme ideas about changing society | Maths signs | Old castles
test: In science, a free radical is an atom that | *reacts easily | is a big rock | is asleep | never changes
exam: «The scientist studied a free radical in the lab.» What does free radical mean here? | Slang for excellent | *An atom or group of atoms that reacts easily | A very old castle | A maths root sign
